  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DIHR DEME SO human rights program 2014-2016 - Sida and Danida new strategy</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">DIHR DEME SO m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter 2014-2016</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Programmets bas &#xE4;r verksamheten med barfotajurister, som med stor geografisk t&#xE4;ckning och lokal f&#xF6;rankring assisterar s&#xE5;rbara grupper i att skapa f&#xF6;ruts&#xE4;ttningar f&#xF6;r &#xE5;tnjutandet av grundl&#xE4;ggande medborgerliga r&#xE4;ttigheter och tillg&#xE5;ng till r&#xE4;ttslig pr&#xF6;vning. Barfotajuristerna fungerar ocks&#xE5; som en sorts brygga mellan det informella och formella r&#xE4;ttssystemet s&#xE5;tillvida att de &#xE4;ven medlar i konflikter inom familjer som ofta kan l&#xF6;sas genom f&#xF6;rlikning utan att tas genom det formella r&#xE4;ttssystemet. Programmet st&#xE4;rker &#xE4;ven s&#xE5;rbara gruppers tillg&#xE5;ng till r&#xE4;ttslig pr&#xF6;vning genom sitt centra f&#xF6;r r&#xE4;ttshj&#xE4;lp (clinique juridique) i Bamako och sina tv&#xE5; juridiska informationkontor (centre d&apos;assistance juridique et judiciaire) i Bamako och S&#xE9;gou. Vid ett kvinnof&#xE4;ngelse i Bamako bedriver man kapacitetsbyggande verksamhet med f&#xE5;ngarna. Den r&#xF6;da tr&#xE5;den i programmet &#xE4;r &#xF6;kad tillg&#xE5;ng till r&#xE4;ttvisa, r&#xE4;ttigheter och r&#xE4;ttslig pr&#xF6;vning f&#xF6;r s&#xE5;rbara grupper, samt &#xF6;kad m&#xF6;jlighet till samh&#xE4;lleligt deltagande.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The base of the program are the paralegals, who with a wide geographic coverage and solid local connection enable vulnerable groups to enjoy basic civil rights and access to justice. The paralegals also function as a bridge between the informal and formal legal systems inasmuch as they mediate in conflicts within families which can commonly be resolved through settlements without being taken to the formal justice system. The program also strengthen vulnerable group&apos;s access to justice through their legal aid clinic in Bamako and their two legal information offices in Bamako and S&#xE9;gou. At a prison for women in Bamako the program have capacity building acitivities with the inmates. The silver thread in the program is  access to justice and rights for vulnerable groups, and increased citizen participation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To offer legal aid to vulnerable groups and to promote citizen participation in the areas of intervention.</narrative>
  </description>
